---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import CtaBand from "../../components/CtaBand.astro";
import FaqList from "../../components/FaqList.astro";

const faq = [
  {
    q: "When does relapse-prevention planning start?",
    a: "During residential treatment — not the Friday of discharge. Case management and clinicians write the next step: people, places, medications when indicated, outpatient care, and what to do in the first bad week home.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is relapse a failure?",
    a: "Relapse is a setback and a clinical event, not a moral verdict. If withdrawal is underway again, medical detox may be needed. The plan is revised; it is not torn up.",
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Relapse Prevention in Residential Treatment"
  description="Relapse prevention in Orange County during residential care in Santa Ana — triggers, aftercare, and a written next step. Starts before discharge."
  path="/services/relapse-prevention/"
  keywords="relapse prevention Orange County, aftercare drug rehab Santa Ana, relapse triggers recovery"
  faq={faq}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Services", path: "/services/" },
    { name: "Relapse prevention", path: "/services/relapse-prevention/" },
  ]}
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/services/">Services</a> / Relapse prevention</p>
      <p class="kicker">Services</p>
      <h1>Relapse prevention in Orange County, CA</h1>
      <p class="lede">A residential stay without a next step is a pause. Relapse prevention is the written plan: people, places, medications when indicated, outpatient care, and what to do in the first bad week home.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Recognizing relapse triggers</h2>
      <p>Relapse is often described as a return to a former state — not only the physical act of using. Emotional relapse (isolation, resentment, dropping the plan) can arrive first. Triggers are the people, places, songs, shifts, and paydays that used to pair with use. The work is to name them while you still have a campus between you and them.</p>
      <h2>What to expect here</h2>
      <p>Plans are individual, written with a therapist and case manager, and revised when they fail a real week. Coping skills, family involvement when useful, and a next level of care are part of the same document. If withdrawal starts again, <a href="/programs/detox/">detox</a> is available. If the environment at home is the problem, <a href="/programs/residential/">residential treatment</a> is the setting where the plan is built.</p>
      <h2>Benefits of a written strategy</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A named list of triggers instead of a vague promise to “be careful”</li>
        <li>People who can be called — family, peers, a clinician — before the use</li>
        <li>Support groups when they fit the person, not as a slogan</li>
        <li>Sleep, food, and movement as part of the plan, not decoration</li>
      </ul>
      <p>See also our article <a href="/blog/strategies-for-relapse-prevention/">Strategies for Relapse Prevention</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <FaqList items={faq} />
    </div>
  </section>
  <CtaBand />
</Base>
